# /usr/lib/powos-steam/steam-env: environment for Steam and EVERY game it starts (native Linux builds and Proton
# alike: Steam's children inherit it, pressure-vessel passes it into the container, FEX reads FEX_* as its config).
# /usr/bin/steam exports each KEY=VALUE line; ~/.config/powos/steam-env (same format) comes after and wins, an empty
# value there (KEY=) unsets a default. Applies from Steam's next start. Measured with tools/phone/verify/bf-coldstart.sh
# (env:KEY=VALUE tokens) before a line goes in here.
#
# Candidates being measured (2026-10-23, Broforce + Teardown):
#   PRESSURE_VESSEL_GENERATE_LOCALES=0   the container's locale-gen (pv-locale-gen under FEX) for the session's
#                                        LANG=en_CH.UTF-8, which games run with LC_ALL=C anyway
#   FEX_ENABLECODECACHINGWIP=1           FEX keeps the x86 code it compiled (per game, compatdata/<id>/fex-emu)

# HACK: GL_ARB_buffer_storage on the phone's freedreno: the lfdevs Mesa (freedreno_screen.c fd_init_screen_caps) turns
# buffer_map_persistent_coherent off on KGSL ("KGSL mappings are not coherent"), so GL stops at 4.3 without
# ARB_buffer_storage; a game that calls glBufferStorage anyway jumps to NULL (Teardown 1167630: crash at
# teardown.exe+0x5BCD63 creating its first uniform buffer, black window). Native KGSL BOs are write-combined
# (uncached, coherent); only dma-heap shared/scanout BOs are cached. Measured 2026-10-23 08:51 (td-launch arm64 with
# this line): no crash, Teardown draws its splash. Real fix: a PowOS Mesa build with the cap kept for native BOs
# (only shared dma-heap BOs need the cache maintenance), then this line goes.
MESA_EXTENSION_OVERRIDE=+GL_ARB_buffer_storage

# HACK: no System V IPC in native (Linux build) games: Android's kernel has none (semget -> ENOSYS) and the sysvipc
# shim /usr/bin/steam preloads never reaches them - the game process's LD_PRELOAD is empty under Valve's FEX compat
# tool + pressure-vessel (bf-coldstart hang_diag, 2026-10-23 10:36). Unity's old Mono retries semget forever in its
# runtime init: Broforce native spun 4 min at 100% with no window (gdb: FEX's raw svc 190 every sample). Mono without
# its shared-handle segment needs no semaphores. Measured 10:31: Broforce native window 36.6 s, first frame 44.9 s.
# Real fix: the x86_64 shim inside native games (pass it through the FEX compat tool / pressure-vessel), then this goes.
MONO_DISABLE_SHM=1

# HACK: FEX's Vulkan thunk for x86 games (x86 Proton, native Linux builds): their Vulkan calls go to PowOS's own
# aarch64 loader + Turnip (vulkan-freedreno-kgsl, patched, native) instead of FEX RootFS's x86_64 Turnip run under
# emulation. /usr/bin/steam's STEAM_COMPAT_FEX_CONFIG (ThunksDB_Vulkan:1) never reaches a game: the client sets that
# variable itself, to its per-game FEX setting (empty), for every launch (fex-compat-tool's printenv log,
# /tmp/fex-compat-tool-<pid>.log: STEAM_COMPAT_FEX_CONFIG=, 2026-11-04), so Valve's FEX compat tool wrote an empty
# ThunksDB and Broforce mapped the RootFS Turnip (bf-driver.sh). FEX_THUNKCONFIG (FEX's ThunkConfig option, read from
# the environment) is a layer the client doesn't touch; FEX resolves /usr/... to /run/host/usr/... inside
# pressure-vessel itself. ThunksDB.json's overlays already cover the container's loader paths
# (/usr/lib/pressure-vessel/overrides/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu). A per-game Steam FEX setting, when set, still wins.
# Real fix: the client honouring STEAM_COMPAT_FEX_CONFIG from its environment (Valve), then this line goes.
FEX_THUNKCONFIG=/usr/lib/powos-steam/fex-thunks.json

# HACK: PowOS's sitecustomize.py (pkgs/steam/sitecustomize.py, in /usr/lib/powos-steam/py) for Valve's FEX compat
# tool, the first layer of every x86 Proton launch: it skips the install script evaluator Steam runs before EVERY
# launch when it has nothing to do, before FEX, the Steam Runtime container and Proton start (7-33 s a launch,
# Broforce 2026-11-04; see that file and user_settings.py). Any other Python under Steam imports it too and it
# returns at once. Real fix: Valve's client skipping an evaluator run it already ran in this prefix, then this line
# and sitecustomize.py go.
PYTHONPATH=/usr/lib/powos-steam/py
